# Selected Hyperparameters

This document records the **final (best) hyperparameters** chosen per dataset and
model after the 65/15/20 temporal-split grid search (grid search on the 15 %
validation set. These are the values that should be used to retrain each model on the
train+val split and report final results on the held-out 20 % test set.

---


### Hyperparameter glossary

| Parameter | Applies to | Meaning |
|-----------|-----------|---------|
| **Batch_Size**      | all | Mini-batch size during training. |
| **Learning_Rate**   | all | Optimiser learning rate. |
| **Dropout**         | D-TAIA, Oyamada | Dropout rate in the encoder / hidden layers. |
| **Hidden_Dim**      | MT-RNN | Recurrent hidden state size (per direction). |
| **Num_Layers**      | MT-RNN | Number of stacked recurrent layers. |
| **RT_Loss_Weight**  | D-TAIA, MT-RNN | Weight of the remaining-time MSE loss relative to the NA cross-entropy (α / `rt_weight` / `mt_weight`). |
| **Triplet_Weight**  | D-TAIA | Weight λ of the domain-aware triplet loss. |
| **Triplet_Margin**  | D-TAIA | Margin τ in the domain-aware triplet loss. |
| **LoRA_Rank**       | FT-LLM | LoRA adapter rank `r`. |
| **LoRA_Alpha**      | LoRA scaling factor α. |
| **LoRA_Dropout**    | Dropout inside the LoRA adapters. |

`N/A` = the parameter does not apply to that model on that dataset.

---

